Owner-approved governance edit (2026-09-01): .githooks/** and AGENTS.md
require human approval, granted explicitly along with self-merge via
auto-pr.

THE DEFECT. DEFAULT_CORE_FILES grew a third entry (io_boundary.py) while
.githooks/pre-commit still fired the axis-declaration check on
^packages/.*/src/.*/(ir|datamodels)\.py$. Staging only io_boundary.py
therefore printed "skipped" over a file the constant said was in scope —
visible in WI-mubup's own commit output. CI was never affected:
test_live_tree_passes runs find_field_drift over every scoped file
regardless of staging. The local fast-feedback path was the narrow one, and
a gate that prints "skipped" is easy to read past.

THE REGEX FIX ALONE WOULD HAVE BEEN THE WRONG DELIVERABLE, because the same
drift recurs the next time a file joins the constant — the hook and the
constant are two homes for one fact, which is the shape this whole campaign
exists to remove. So the deliverable is the agreement test:
test_the_precommit_hook_regex_covers_every_scoped_core_file parses the
alternation out of the hook and asserts it covers every stem in
DEFAULT_CORE_FILES.

PROVED TO FIRE RATHER THAN ASSUMED: narrowing the regex back to
(ir|datamodels) fails the test; restoring it passes. And the live hook was
exercised on a staged io_boundary.py alone, which now runs the check
instead of skipping it.

AGENTS.md's essentialization named the same two files and is updated with
the regex, including the two new registry-backed axis names (io-boundary /
module-key per ADR-0050 / ADR-0051) in its list of valid categories.

1,759 tests pass, mypy ratchet clean.

